WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
English has three ways to look back.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.970
'I used to have a dog.' 'I was watching

3
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.660
TV.' 'It was great.' Now the French.

4
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.220
«Je regardais la télé.» «C'était
génial.» Two different verbs,

5
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.400
saying two different kinds of thing.

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.350
But listen to how they end.

7
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.590
So how can French cover 'used to',

8
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.460
'was doing' and 'it was'
with just one tense?

9
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.670
In this mission, you'll lay
the past out on a timeline,

10
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.390
one memory at a time.

11
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.490
Then you'll paint a day at the beach:

12
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.560
the weather, a café, and how you felt.

13
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.000
Your mission: find out how
French builds this tense,

14
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.430
and use it to bring any memory to life.
